{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 35, :comments ["<b>And Moses was not able.</b> Then HaShem called him to enter the tent and he would speak with HaShem face to face in the place where the high priest would enter once a year with the cloud of incense, for Moses is a member of the household. And I needed to say thus, for Moses placed the tablets in the ark, and there was the cover upon which the cherubim are, upon the ark, and upon them always the Glory. Now what would happen when Aaron and his sons take down the curtain-screen from outside the place of the ark — how would they approach it? Therefore I said that Moses alone would enter within the curtain, and Aaron and his sons would take down the screen called curtain, and Moses would take the screen and immediately cover with it the ark of the testimony, so that Aaron and his sons would not see it. And Scripture says וכסו בו (and they covered with it), for they would assist him. And some say that the priests cover the ark while their faces are not toward the ark. And because it is written concerning it ואש תהיה לילה בו (and fire by night in it) (Exodus [parashat] 38), and it says לכל מסעיהם (for all their journeys) — this too indicates that there are times when the cloud would travel by night. But we have not found written that they traveled by night, and the one who says this will interpret יומם ולילה (by day and by night) as one day. But then what does he do with the word מסעיהם (their journeys), and it does not say מחניהם (their camps)? Rather its meaning is: either by day and by night, or by day or by night, like ומקלל אביו ואמו מות יומת (and one who curses his father or his mother shall surely be put to death) (above 21:17). And I needed all this because I saw written in Moses's prayer concerning the matter of the spies: ובעמוד ענן אתה הולך לפניהם יומם, ובעמוד אש לילה (and in a pillar of cloud You go before them by day, and in a pillar of fire by night) (Numbers 14:14)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 40, :notes {0 "The citation '(פ׳ לח)' likely refers to Numbers 9:15–16 (parashat Beha'alotekha), not Exodus 38, since Exodus 38 does not contain the quoted phrase; resolving as ambiguous and translating the reference as given."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:41:05.440935165Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}